  "mechanismSummary": "tert-Butoxide deprotonates trimethylsulfonium iodide to give dimethylsulfonium methylide. The ylide adds to the ketone, and the alkoxide formed displaces dimethyl sulfide in an intramolecular SN2, giving an epoxide. Compare the Wittig: there oxygen bonds to phosphorus because P=O is strong; here sulfur is a good leaving group instead. The more stable dimethylsulfoxonium methylide (from Me₃S⁺=O I⁻) adds reversibly and, with an enone, does conjugate addition to give a cyclopropane.",
